course: dictionary
lesson: 14307
title: Nutritious: food that helps you grow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some foods are full of the things your body needs to grow and stay healthy, such as vitamins, protein and minerals. We call these foods nutritious. «Oats, banana and milk make a nutritious breakfast.» The clue is that the food is good for your body, so nutritious must mean healthy and full of good things.
explain: Look at the words around nutritious. «Crisps are tasty, but they are not very nutritious.» The word but tells you that the crisps are one thing and the nutrition is another: they taste good, but they do not give your body much that it needs. So a nutritious food is one that helps your body, not just one that tastes nice.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Eggs and fish are nutritious, so they help your body grow strong.» If you swap in full of what your body needs, the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Nutritious means full of the things your body needs to grow and stay healthy.
fact: Vitamins, protein and minerals are all things that make food nutritious.
fact: In a balanced diet, nutritious foods include fruit, vegetables, whole grains, beans, eggs and fish.
fact: «A nutritious breakfast» means a breakfast that is good for your body, such as porridge with fruit.
fact: Nutritious and healthy are close in meaning, but nutritious focuses on the good things food gives your body.
exercise: «Oats, fruit and milk make a nutritious breakfast.» What does nutritious mean? | Cold enough to keep in the fridge | Very sweet and sticky | Expensive to buy | *Full of what your body needs to grow and stay healthy
exercise: Which of these is a nutritious food? | *Carrots | Sweets | Crisps | Fizzy cola
exercise: «Eggs and fish are nutritious, so they help your body grow strong.» What does nutritious mean here? | *Full of what your body needs | Very expensive | Full of sugar | Cooked in a pan
test: Mum says, «Pick a nutritious snack, not a sugary one.» Which snack is nutritious? | Sweets | Crisps | *Apple slices | Chocolate biscuit
test: Which phrase uses nutritious correctly? | A nutritious bicycle | A nutritious football match | *A nutritious breakfast of eggs and fruit | A nutritious puddle on the road
exam: Why do parents want children to eat nutritious meals? | So children can skip school | *So children grow and stay healthy | To save money on shopping | To make the kitchen smell nice
